    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/how-to-apply/finding-a-role-and-applying-online": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Finding a role and applying online | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs How to apply Finding a role and applying online Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Finding a role and applying online Section - Jobs How to apply Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Jobs home Why Cambridge? Browse our vacancies Life in Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge Search all University jobs Finding a role Our vacancies are broadly split across three categories: Academic Research , and Professional services , which covers our operational support roles. You can search for roles by category to find the type of job you’re looking for. Applying online Just click the ‘apply now’ button on the job advert. You’ll need to enter your email address to register for our online system, and guidance is available to help you through the process of filling out the online application. Each job advert will give you a summary of the role, key information like the salary, closing date and reference number, and a ‘further information’ document. The job advert (or further information document) will tell you who to contact if you have any questions about the job. You can also contact that person should you need the application in a different format, for example, if you have a disability. In some limited circumstances, there may not be the option to apply online for a vacancy. The job advert (or the further information document) will provide information on how and where to apply. It will also tell you who to contact if you have any questions. If you experience technical difficulties with the online application process, please contact our Technical Support Team at: technical.recruitmentsupport@admin.cam.ac.uk For information about how your personal data is used as an applicant, please see the section on Applicant Data on our HR web pages. Unfortunately we are unable to consider speculative applications for employment, but we do offer work experience and volunteering opportunities. Work experience and volunteering If you are interested in work experience, or opportunities to volunteer with the University of Cambridge, please see: Work experience Volunteer with us Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/how-to-apply/inclusive-recruitment": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Inclusive recruitment | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs How to apply Inclusive recruitment Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Inclusive recruitment Section - Jobs How to apply Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Jobs home Why Cambridge? Browse our vacancies Life in Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge Search all University jobs We believe that embracing inclusivity enhances our collective impact. As an employer, we foster equality and inclusion, and by joining us, you will become part of a vibrant, talented, and creative global community. Information if you have a disability As a proud member of the Disability Confident scheme, the University of Cambridge welcomes applications from individuals with disabilities. We will ensure fair treatment throughout the recruitment process, and adjust the process wherever reasonable, to enable applicants to compete to the best of their ability – and continue to support you through your employment. We do not provide our recruiting teams with any information about a candidate’s protected characteristics, including disability. If you would like to be considered under the Disability Confident scheme, we encourage candidates to state this under the 'Reasonable Adjustments' section of the application. This information is only available to recruitment administrators. We encourage applicants to disclose their disabilities in the ‘Equal Opportunities Monitoring’ section of the application. Applicants or employees can disclose a disability at any time. If you wish to discuss any reasonable adjustments, you can contact the recruiting department at any point in the process. Contact details will be in the job advert or the further information document (which will be attached to the vacancy). Alternatively, you can contact the HR Resourcing Team . We have dedicated web pages for applicants and employees with a disability . If you cannot apply online—for example, if you have a disability—then you should contact the person listed on the advert, who will be able to provide you with an application in another suitable alternative format. Equal opportunities monitoring As part of the application process, we may ask some questions about you to help us monitor how well our equal opportunities policy is working. We may ask about your race, ethnicity, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation and whether you have any disabilities. We use these categories as outlined by the Higher Education Statistics Agency (HESA). We recognise the sensitivity of this information and we only use it in the manner set out above, to generate anonymised and aggregated equality statistics. This information is stored in a different part of our system. It will not be visible when you or others view your application, and it will not be used as part of the selection process. We encourage all applicants to complete this section of the application as fully as possible, but each question also has a “Prefer not to say” option for those who do not feel comfortable to share this information. For information about how applicants’ personal data is used, please see the section on Applicant Data on our HR web pages. Equal Opportunities Policy The University's Combined Equality Scheme (PDF) The University’s Diversity Networks Rehabilitation of Offenders Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/how-to-apply/application-tips": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Application tips | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs How to apply Application tips Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Application tips Section - Jobs How to apply Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Jobs home Why Cambridge? Browse our vacancies Life in Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge Search all University jobs Here are some tips to help you put your best foot forward when applying for a role at the University of Cambridge. Education history List your complete educational history, even qualifications that are not related directly to the role. Have an overseas qualification? You can check how it corresponds to UK qualifications (e.g. GCSE, A Level) at http://www.naric.org.uk/ . Some roles require a qualification “or equivalent experience”. Where applicable, this will be clarified in the Person Specification. Career history List your full career history, including voluntary roles and work experience, to demonstrate the full range of your experience and your transferable skills. For each role, include: Employer Name, Job Title, Start Date, and End Date. Enter the main parts of your job. Keep this brief and highlight the tasks and achievements relevant to the role you are applying for. Enter the reason for leaving that role (e.g. ‘Relocation’). Detail your current or most recent employment/experience first and work backwards. Please mention significant breaks in employment, such as travelling, periods of unemployment or voluntary work. Suitability for the role / cover letters: This section is your opportunity to tell us why you think you would suit the role you’re applying for. Use the ‘Person Specification’, which can be found in the Further Information document, as a guide of what to include. This highlights the skills and experience we are looking for. Note: Avoid simply duplicating the person specification without explaining your experience in each area. Focus on the role you want to apply for, providing specific details on why your experience is appropriate for the role. Where possible, provide brief and specific examples from your work, education or other experience that show that you have the knowledge and skills required. Mention any transferrable skills and experience that might be relevant to the role, especially if you are looking to change career. Don’t feel the need to include too much here (up to a maximum of 2 A4 sides is plenty). References Please provide the details of three referees for academic and research roles, and at least two previous employers for Professional Services roles. The online recruitment system will tell you how many references are required for the role that you are applying for. You should not list relatives or friends as referees unless they have employed you and you do not have any other previous employers. It is essential that you indicate at what point you would be happy for us to contact each referee. This can be at any time during the selection process, when you have been invited to interview, or after you have accepted any conditional offer of employment. For Professional Services roles, on referee must be your current (or most recent) employer. If you do not have a previous employer, you can use educational references. Uploading documents Certain vacancies will require you to provide us with documents such as a Curriculum Vitae and covering letter in the Upload section of the application form. Details of the documents that you need to provide will be given in the advert and/or Further Information document for the vacancy. The documents that you upload must be in .pdf format. Other types of files will not be accepted by the system. A maximum of 5 files may be attached per application. You will have a chance to review the document(s) before submitting your application. Please check that: Files are not password protected The documents are clear and legible Documents do not contain any macros or other executable code; and Documents are not read-only files. Please only upload requested documents. Any additional documents will not be considered as part of the application process. Submitting your application After entering/uploading the information required as part of the application, you will reach a summary page. This page will show you all sections of the application and where more information is required (which will be denoted with a * symbol. You can go back through your application as required. If all steps have been completed, review your application and click “Submit”. We will be in touch to confirm the outcome of your application shortly after the closing date. Please note: You will not be able to change your application once you have submitted it. If you are expecting any details in your application to change before the closing date of a vacancy, you may wish to delay submitting your application. If you have any general queries about the application process, please contact the Resourcing Team . 