    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/browse-our-vacancies/academic-vacancies/working-as-an-academic-at-cambridge": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Working as an academic at Cambridge | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Browse our vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Working as an academic at Cambridge Section - Jobs Browse our vacancies Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? How to apply Life in Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge Search all University jobs Thinking about Cambridge for your next career move? With its blend of tradition, intellectual exploration and a strong sense of community, the academic experience at University of Cambridge is uniquely fulfilling. Key to this experience are the twin environments of department and college life. Cambridge’s 31 independent colleges are communities where students and staff alike find academic support and social interaction, and where our famous small-group teaching takes place. Whether it’s dining in historic – or contemporary - halls, hosting interdisciplinary conferences, or debating the theories of the day with brilliant colleagues, the collegiate system is truly unique. Lectures and group research take place in more than 100 faculties, departments and institutions. There are also strategic research initiatives and interdisciplinary research centres that tackle challenges that can only be addressed by multi-disciplinary teams of researchers. The University offers unparalleled opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. Academics and researchers enjoy high levels of autonomy, with freedom to explore their interests unrestricted. They also have world-class resources at their fingertips – including one of the largest libraries in the world. Cambridge students are some of the brightest and most motivated in the world. Through the supervision system of one-to-one and small-group teaching, academics really get to know their students, pushing them to be the best they can be intellectually. We are proud of offering our students the chance to study with leading academics, and teaching loads allow plenty of research time. Ideas and innovation thrive at Cambridge and we offer excellent support to research spin-outs, helping turn groundbreaking ideas into impactful businesses through Cambridge Enterprise. With students, researchers, academics and faculty from more than 140 countries, Cambridge is host to a rich diversity of new ideas and cultural experiences, both inside the lecture hall and out. This vibrancy spills over into the city as a whole, which buzzes with talks, debates, lectures, concerts and performances - all against a backdrop of stunning architecture, historic streets, peaceful green spaces, and of course the serene and picturesque River Cam. Learn more about living in Cambridge As an academic at the University of Cambridge, you can expect: Annual progression schemes on both our Research and Teaching, and Teaching and Scholarship pathways (or our biennial progression scheme for Professors (Grade 12). Sabbatical leave at the rate of one term for every six terms of service. Access to resources from the Cambridge Centre for Teaching and Learning A new self-match mentoring scheme for academic staff. View current academic vacancies Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
