bridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Section - Jobs Browse our vacancies Academic vacancies Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? How to apply Life in Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge Search all University jobs Cambridge has given rise to many pathbreaking ideas, discoveries and breakthroughs that are helping shape the future on a global scale. Everyone who works here contributes to these achievements. Our professional staff – whether an IT specialist, a librarian, a college porter or catering assistant – all play a role in helping us achieve our academic mission. At Cambridge, you’ll join a diverse, talented and innovative community of more than 13,000 staff from all backgrounds and corners of the world. Here’s what makes working at Cambridge special: You can take pride in our prestigious global reputation, and in the real impact we have on the world around us You will feel part of a welcoming and collaborative community where  professional expertise is valued and recognised You will be able to maintain your work-life balance with flexible working arrangements, family-friendly policies and other initiatives to support your wellbeing in and out of the workplace You will be part of an inclusive, dynamic and diverse workforce made up of people from all cultures and walks of life You will enjoy beautiful surroundings – spectacular architecture, cobbled streets steeped in history, striking modern developments and stunning green spaces We offer a wide range of support to our staff to help them progress in their fields, including: In-house training courses including career-development, leadership and management Apprenticeships leading to qualifications directly relevant to your role Reimbursement for the cost of professional membership fees A wide range of programmes delivered by Professional and Continuing Education (PACE) – many with a 25% concession for University staff Reduced staff fees for University of Cambridge graduate courses Plenty of opportunity to attend lectures and seminars hosted by University departments and institutions. Access to our annual contribution reward scheme, which offers pay progression for continued achievement in your role. This is supplemented by our annual awards event, further celebrating the contributions of our staff. View current professional services vacancies Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
