      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Life in Cambridge | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Life in Cambridge Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Life in Cambridge Section - Jobs Life in Cambridge Community and surroundings Getting around Jobs home Why Cambridge? How to apply Browse our vacancies Relocating to Cambridge Search all University jobs Spectacular architecture, modern amenities and beautiful outdoor spaces all tucked together in a convenient and compact city make Cambridge a uniquely appealing place. With good links to London, reliable public transport, a car-free centre and well-maintained bike paths, it’s easy to get around sustainably. In fact, Cambridge is the cycling capital of the UK, with more than 55% of locals cycling at least once a week. The city is well-served by healthcare facilities including Addenbrooke’s Hospital, which is also a leading centre for medical research. Families have a range of options to ensure their children get a quality education. Cambridge offers a strong network of state-funded primary and secondary schools rated “good” or “outstanding” by Ofsted, as well as prestigious independent schools and even schools that specifically aim to provide an international curriculum. Cambridge punches above its weight culturally, with concert halls, theatres, libraries, museums and galleries. And in the summer, the city’s many parks and meadows are perfect for picnics or walks, while the slow and serene River Cam offers boating options from rowing to kayaking, paddleboarding and punting. Learn more Community and surroundings Getting around Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
