e Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Accommodation and relocation support Section - Jobs Relocating to Cambridge Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Jobs home Why Cambridge? How to apply Browse our vacancies Life in Cambridge Search all University jobs What's family life like at the University of Cambridge? New to Cambridge? We have a range of support to make the move and transition easier for new employees: Eligible employees (subject to the completion of an eligibility questionnaire) can claim back up to £8,000 of relocation expenses, tax-free. Our rental deposit loan scheme can help with some of the costs of private rental accommodation, like initial deposit, firs month’s rent and fees. Our shared equity scheme means eligible employees can get financial assistance to purchase a house in the Cambridge area. We can help you find short-, medium- and long-term accommodation if you’re new to Cambridge (or the UK). Our Accommodation Service lets University-owned properties, and advertises rooms, apartments, and houses from private landlords. And we can help you settle in even further with our Newcomers and Visiting Scholars Group , which welcomes the partners and families of visiting scholars and hosts events like coffee hours, walking tours lectures and cinema visits. Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
