    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/associate-director-physical-sciences-permanent-and-maternity-cover-dh50680": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Physical Sciences (Permanent and Maternity Cover)",
      "description": "Associate Director, Physical Sciences (Permanent and Maternity Cover) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Associate Director, Physical Sciences (Permanent and Maternity Cover) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Associate Director, Physical Sciences (Permanent and Maternity Cover) Are you interested in securing some of the most influential donations of your career? Would you like to work in an environment with significant fundraising opportunities and an extensive pool of potential donors, with the chance to secure gifts at the 6, 7 and even 8-figure level? We are delighted to be recruiting two experienced fundraisers to join our team fundraising for the School of the Physical Sciences: one permanent position and one maternity cover position. You will be fundraising for one of the University's largest and most exciting Schools, working alongside world-leading academics and engaging with an international community of donors and prospects. A background in science is not required. Many of our science fundraisers come from humanities and other non-scientific backgrounds. What matters is your ability to build trusted relationships, develop compelling opportunities for support and confidently pursue major gifts that can help turn bold ideas into reality. Why this role? Why now? This is an exciting time to join the Physical Sciences fundraising portfolio. There is already significant momentum, with a robust pipeline of active donor conversations and prospective opportunities progressing well. Whether you join us in the permanent position or on a maternity cover basis, you will step into an established portfolio where relationships are developing and opportunities are taking shape, allowing you to make an impact from the outset. The maternity cover role will offer the opportunity to build relationships, shape compelling proposals and potentially bring several significant gifts to a successful conclusion during the period of cover, while the permanent role offers the opportunity to develop the portfolio and relationships over the longer term. You'll work closely with visionary academics to develop cases for support and lead the cultivation of major donors who want to fund innovation at scale. What you'll do: Lead strategy and delivery for major gift fundraising across the School. \nManage and cultivate a portfolio of 50 - 90 donors and prospects, focusing on gifts between £100k and £5m. \nBuild strong partnerships with leading researchers and internal stakeholders. \nTravel in the UK to engage major donors and prospects. \nCollaborate across Cambridge's collegiate development network to maximise impact. Who we're looking for: We're seeking a confident, curious and collaborative professional with a strong track record in high-value fundraising or relationship management. If you thrive on meaningful conversations, enjoy a challenge and bring strategic thinking to complex opportunities, we'd love to hear from you. You'll have: Experience in major gifts fundraising or managing high-level stakeholder relationships. Strong verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to inspire and influence. Emotional intelligence, resilience and an entrepreneurial mindset. A commitment to equity, inclusion and working with integrity. Why join Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations? Working here means joining a talented, mission-driven community helping unlock the potential of one of the world's most influential universities. A meaningful mission Your work will help enable discoveries, expand access to education and support research that improves lives locally and globally. A leading fundraising environment You'll be part of a respected advancement team, with excellent infrastructure, systems and networks to support your success. Growth and learning With mentoring, secondments, structured learning and access to Cambridge's intellectual community, we support your professional development and advancement career. Wellbeing and balance Flexible working, generous leave and wellbeing resources help you thrive professionally and personally. Diversity and belonging We value different voices and lived experiences and aim to create an environment where everyone feels included and supported. Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations - Do your best work here. Apply online Download further information Candidate Pack - Associate Director, Physical Sciences (Permanent and Maternity Cover) Key information Department/location University of Cambridge Development and Alumni Relations Salary £47,389-£59,966 Reference DH50680 Category Academic-related Date published 11 August 2026 Closing date 6 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
