    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/business-administration-apprentice-x-2-ew49664": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Business Administration Apprentice x 2 | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Business Administration Apprentice x 2 Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Business Administration Apprentice x 2 The Research Office is seeking to recruit two Business Administration Apprentices to join our new Business Support Function. This is a fantastic opportunity to gain experience in a variety of areas and a qualification that will create a firm foundation for a future career in administration As part of the Business Support Function, you will provide administrative and operational support across the Research Office. Working within a collaborative team, you will contribute to a wide range of activities and projects across Research Services, helping to deliver high-quality support services to colleagues across the department. The role offers the opportunity to gain experience across a variety of business support activities, supporting colleagues in different areas of the Research Office whilst studying to complete a Business and Administration Level 3 Qualification using the skills and knowledge you have built up to complete your projects and assignments. You should hold GCSE qualifications (or equivalent) in English and Mathematics at Grade C/4 or above. You will have experience using basic IT applications, including word processing, spreadsheets and email systems, together with strong organisational, communication and time-management skills. We are looking for enthusiastic individuals with a willingness to learn, a positive approach and an interest in developing a career in business support and administration. The University is unable to provide sponsorship under the Skilled Worker visa route for this role, as it does not meet the minimum skill and/or salary requirements. All applications are being managed by the training provider. To apply for this post, please use this link to access the National Apprenticeship Service site and follow the on-screen instructions on how to submit your application: https://www.findapprenticeship.service.gov.uk/apprenticeship/VAC2000050028 Please quote reference EW49664 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Cambridge Research Office Salary £20,058 Reference EW49664 Category Assistant staff Date published 26 August 2026 Closing date 20 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
