    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/careers-consultant-temporary-cover-dd49764": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Careers Consultant [Temporary Cover] | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Careers Consultant [Temporary Cover] Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Careers Consultant [Temporary Cover] Temporary cover: This post is fixed-term for 10 months or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. The University of Cambridge Careers Service is seeking to appoint a Careers Consultant on a 10 month fixed term contract to cover a period of maternity leave.\nPrimarily responsible for providing careers education, advice and guidance to PhD candidates and Postdoctoral Research staff. This role would be particularly suitable for candidates with an understanding of the career challenges faced by early career researchers (within and beyond academia). They will also contribute to the programme of activity supporting students at all levels. The role will also take over the stakeholder management of Departments (within Clinical Medicine and Biological Science disciplines) and Colleges that the current role holder is responsible for. Providing the expertise, experience and tools to help shape delivery for local activities designed to support individuals' career development. \nThe ideal candidate will be fascinated by the evolving Labour Market, experienced with digital delivery, and an excellent communicator capable of building and sustaining relationships across the Collegiate University and beyond. Previous experience of careers work in a Higher Education setting, experience of graduate recruitment or similar professional experience is essential. More detailed information on the role can be found in the Further Particulars document, via the link at the bottom of this advert. We are able to accommodate flexible working arrangements, including compressed hours or part-time working patterns of 0.8 FTE and above for this role. Benefits of working at the University of Cambridge include: Competitive rates of pay with automatic service-related pay progression and annual cost of living increases; Generous annual leave allowance; Flexible and hybrid working opportunities; Generous maternity, adoption and shared parental leave entitlement and other family friendly schemes (e.g. workplace nurseries); An auto-enrolment pension scheme, with a generous employer contribution; Travel benefits and retail discounts at over 2,000 local and national stores; Schemes to support with relocation / the provision of accommodation. Additional information regarding the role can be found within the Further Particulars. \nWhen applying, please upload your CV and cover letter which clearly sets out how you meet the criteria listed in the person specification of the Further Particulars (the knowledge, skills, and experience required for the role) along with relevant examples. Candidates will be shortlisted and invited to interview based upon these criteria. Applications are welcome from both external and internal candidates including those who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. If you wish to make an informal enquiry, or have any questions about the post, please contact Krista Cooper at kc510@cam.ac.uk . If you have any technical difficulties submitting your online application, please contact the recruitment team - sscjobs@admin.cam.ac.uk Closing date for applications: Sunday 6th September Interview date: Thursday 17th September (only apply if you are available to interview on this date) Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact SSCjobs@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference DD49764 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Careers Service Salary £47,389-£59,966 Reference DD49764 Category Academic-related Date published 26 August 2026 Closing date 6 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
