    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/collections-and-participation-fixed-term-pe50866": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Collections and Participation (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Collections and Participation (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Collections and Participation (Fixed Term) We are looking for a Research Associate to join Collections-Connections-Communities (CCC), a Strategic Research Initiative at the University of Cambridge which empowers researchers to use the University's collections ¿ the UK's highest concentration of internationally important collections outside London ¿ to address the big questions of our time. This is a fixed-term post within a new Collections & Participation team, funded for one year in the first instance with potential for future funding to July 2030, dedicated to bringing communities ¿ especially those that are underrepresented or underserved ¿ into research and practice within the University's collections. You will work alongside a Programmes Coordinator, a Research Associate focused on digital participation, and a Natural History Engagement Coordinator. You will co-design and deliver scalable, ethical, innovative and replicable projects using participatory methodologies, working with new and existing community partners through an agreed framework of ethics and care. You will nurture partnerships with curatorial, conservation, learning and public programmes colleagues, disseminate your work through peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations, and build capacity across the University's collections by offering training in participation methods. You will engage with evidence on community needs across the city and region, prepare funding proposals, monitor budgets, line-manage freelancers, and work with a new Impact & Evaluation team in University of Cambridge Museums to test and refine participation activity. We're looking for someone with experience of co-designing, managing, delivering and evaluating collections-based participation programmes, and research experience with sufficient breadth and depth of specialist knowledge of participatory methodologies, evidenced by peer-reviewed research ¿ which may be co-authored ¿ or by conference papers. Experience of working across multiple collections and stakeholders while navigating conflicting priorities, of line-managing freelancers, and knowledge of ethical frameworks and data protection principles are essential, as is a postgraduate degree or equivalent collections experience of working with communities. A strong commitment to social justice and inclusive practice, and an understanding of Knowledge Exchange and Impact Pathways, would serve you well. This is a rare chance to develop participatory research practice across an entire collections ecosystem rather than a single institution, with an activity budget of your own, a group of mentors with deep experience of participation in collections, and real scope to change practice in the sector. Occasional evening and weekend working will be required alongside the delivery of participation activities. If you'd like to help transform the relationship between Cambridge's collections and the communities around them, we'd love to hear from you. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 1 years in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For any questions relating to this recruitment please contact admin@botanic.cam.ac.uk The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Role Profile/Further information Key information Department/location Botanic Garden Salary £37,694-£46,049 Reference PE50866 Category Academic-related Date published 26 August 2026 Closing date 11 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/coordinator-undergraduate-full-time-maternity-cover-ue50803": {
      "title": "Coordinator [Undergraduate] [Full-time, Maternity Cover]",
      "description": "Coordinator [Undergraduate] [Full-time, Maternity Cover] | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Coordinator [Undergraduate] [Full-time, Maternity Cover] Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Coordinator [Undergraduate] [Full-time, Maternity Cover] Applications are invited for an organised and experienced administrator for the Department of Politics and International Studies (POLIS). This role with a special emphasis on undergraduate programmes. The post holder will be the principal administrator for all POLIS tracks within the HSPS Tripos as well as shared papers on the History and Politics Tripos.  The role has oversight of all administrative elements until final examination and has line management responsibilities. Maternity cover: This post is fixed-term for 12 months or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. The closing date for applications is: Wednesday 09 September 2026. The interview date is expected to be: Week  commencing 21 September 2026 Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to:Business Operations Manager Helen Reynolds BOM@polis.cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact: hr@hsps.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference UE50803 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Politics and International Studies Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference UE50803 Category Assistant staff Date published 20 August 2026 Closing date 9 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
