    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/csca-centre-administrator-part-time-fixed-term-gb50733": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "CSCA Centre Administrator (Part Time, Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs CSCA Centre Administrator (Part Time, Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs CSCA Centre Administrator (Part Time, Fixed Term) The Ax:son Johnson Centre for the Study of Classical Architecture (CSCA) at the Faculty of Architecture and History of Art is seeking a part time (0.6 FTE) Centre Administrator. The Centre was established in 2021 as a collaboration between the two constituent Departments of the University's Faculty of Architecture and History of Art, working with the Faculty of Classics. This role will be fixed term until 30 September 2028 due to limited funding. This role will play a vital part in the day-to-day running of the Centre. The Centre Administrator is a key staff member ensuring the Director, Deputy Director, Visiting Professors, Postdoctoral Research Associates and PhD students receive the operational support they need in order to produce world class research. The role holder will need to work Fridays in term time as well as attend one-off events. During July, the role holder will go to Sweden to support the Summer School. Further information on the centre is available: https://csca.aha.cam.ac.uk/ . Some key responsibilities of the role holder include: Coordinate and oversee the efficient administration of the Centre for the Study of Classical Architecture (CSCA), working closely with the Director. Assist with the production of reports by gathering and analysis of data as required by stakeholders. Be the main point of contact with stakeholders and liaise with them as required. Carry out project financial administration. Process expenses claims. Process invoices. Raise purchase orders and manage purchasing requisitions in accordance with University financial procedures and financial regulations. Maintain accurate records of expenditure against research grants and ratify these with University Central System (CUFS). Check monthly statements and invoices by liaising closely with Departmental Finance office and setting up spreadsheets to facilitate this. Keep a running record of actual expenditure against the relevant budget headings, including for individual Centre staff and students. Organise events such as the regular seminar series and one-off conferences, workshops/ training sessions. Make all necessary arrangements including booking rooms, co-ordinating travel arrangements, liaising with external speakers, arranging catering, and dealing with expense reimbursements.  Provide in-person logistical support at events, both practical and, where appropriate, technological. Informal enquiries about the role are welcomed and should be directed Professor Frank Salmon fes11@cam.ac.uk . For queries about the application process, please contact the School's HR team at sahhr@admin.cam.ac.uk . The closing date for applications is midnight (BST) on Sunday 06 September 2026. Interviews of shortlisted candidates are planned for the week commencing 14 September 2026, subject to change. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference GB50733 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Faculty of Architecture and History of Art Salary £31,236-£35,608 pro rata Reference GB50733 Category Assistant staff Date published 19 August 2026 Closing date 6 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
