    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/cutover-manager-fixed-term-ag50759": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Cutover Manager (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Cutover Manager (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Cutover Manager (Fixed Term) The Cutover Manager plays a critical role in ensuring the programme successfully transitions from implementation into live operation. Your leadership will help deliver a smooth, controlled and well-coordinated deployment, ensuring business readiness, minimising operational risk, and providing confidence that every element of the programme has been planned and executed to the highest standard. Do you have the ability to coordinate multiple workstreams, manage competing priorities, and ensure flawless execution when it matters most? We are looking for an experienced Cutover Manager to lead the planning, coordination and execution of programme deployment activities for a major transformation programme. This is a pivotal role where success depends on your ability to bring structure to complexity, maintain momentum, and ensure every detail has been considered before, during and after go-live. As Cutover Manager, you will have overall responsibility for developing and delivering the programme's cutover strategy and managing the end-to-end deployment lifecycle. From planning and dry runs through to production build and final go-live, you will ensure every activity is carefully coordinated, risks are proactively managed, and operational readiness is achieved across the organisation. This role demands someone with outstanding organisational skills, exceptional attention to detail, and the confidence to challenge, influence and collaborate across technical and business teams to deliver a seamless transition. We're looking for someone who combines excellent programme delivery skills with a meticulous eye for detail.  You'll have: Significant experience managing cutover, deployment or transition activities within large, complex transformation programmes. Outstanding organisational and planning skills, with the ability to manage numerous interdependent activities simultaneously. Exceptional attention to detail, ensuring nothing is overlooked in highly complex deployment plans. Proven experience developing and managing detailed cutover plans across multiple environments. Experience managing risks, issues, dependencies and critical decision points throughout programme delivery. Excellent communication skills with the ability to coordinate diverse technical and business teams under pressure. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Funding for this post is available for 12 months. If you would like more information about this role, informal enquiries can be directed by email to Michelle Bond via Michelle.Bond@admin.cam.ac.uk If you have any questions the application process, please contact a Recruitment Administrator at Finhr_recruitment@admin.cam.ac.uk . The closing date for applications is 09 September 2026. The interviews date for the role are planned 22 September 2026. Please quote reference AG50759 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check, a health assessment and a security check. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Cutover Manager Key information Department/location Finance Division Salary £63,606-£67,468 Reference AG50759 Category Academic-related Date published 14 August 2026 Closing date 9 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
