    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/due-diligence-specialist-2-years-fixed-term-ew49670": {
      "title": "Due Diligence Specialist (2 Years Fixed term)",
      "description": "Due Diligence Specialist (2 Years Fixed term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Due Diligence Specialist (2 Years Fixed term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Due Diligence Specialist (2 Years Fixed term) Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 2 years in the first instance. We are looking for an experienced research and due diligence professional to join the Research Office's Due Diligence team as part of the Governance, Risk and Compliance function. The Research Services Division takes a strategic role in the oversight and development of all aspects of the University's research activities. The Due Diligence team help support researchers working with UK and international organisations to ensure their partnerships do not expose the University to risks, which could undermine the University's academic standing and delivery of its research mission. What will you do? As a Due Diligence Specialist, you will provide targeted analysis to identify and mitigate potential risks associated with third party research engagements and help ensure compliance with relevant legislation associated international engagement and research security. The role will offer the successful applicant the opportunity to: Help safeguard the reputation of the University of Cambridge; Support researchers at the forefront of scientific advancement to navigate complex regulation and risks that come with international research collaboration in an evolving geopolitical landscape; Build specialist research expertise and apply to various regions and sectors; Be part of a growing team in the Governance, Risk and Compliance function; Work within one of the most dynamic and varied research centres in the world. Skills We are looking for a skilled researcher with an interest in legal frameworks and international affairs with excellent analytical and drafting skills The successful candidate should have experience using open-source research tools such as LexisNexis and Factiva, as well as regional and language-specific databases and media sources. Location The University is supportive of hybrid working, where some work is undertaken on university premises and some in a remote working environment. The aim of our approach is to enable as many staff as possible to work in a hybrid way if they wish and where their role allows, with the majority of time spent on-site. The hours of work for the position are full-time with in-person working on Mondays and Thursdays. Informal enquiries should be directed to Rebecca Reid ( rebecca.reid@admin.cam.ac.uk ). Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working (min 80%) or other flexible working arrangements. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please see the Further Particulars document for more details of this vacancy. Your application should clearly set out how you meet the criteria listed in the person specification (the skills and experience required for the role) along with relevant examples. Candidates will be shortlisted based on these criteria. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. The closing date is Sunday 18th October 2026.  It is anticipated interviews will be held in person in Cambridge on the 2nd November 2026. Questions about the application process should be addressed to the Research Office Recruitment team at crorecruitment@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference EW49670 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Cambridge Research Office Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference EW49670 Category Academic-related Date published 1 September 2026 Closing date 19 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/electronics-design-engineer-ka49997": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
