    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/exhibitions-project-manager-da50814": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Exhibitions Project Manager | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Exhibitions Project Manager Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Exhibitions Project Manager The Fitzwilliam Museum: Opening up the past to transform our futures. As the principal museum of the University of Cambridge and the largest cultural venue in the region, The Fitzwilliam Museum acts as a crucial bridge between the University, the City and the rest of the world, and has an international reputation for extraordinary research, world class exhibitions, award-winning public programmes and significant collections spanning many cultures and centuries. The Hamilton Kerr Institute (HKI) is one of the world's leading centres for teaching and research in conservation and heritage science. Temporary exhibitions are where the Museum meets its audiences directly. They are integral to how the Fitzwilliam delivers on its mission and are a core output of its research activities, often involving collaboration with researchers from the wider University and beyond. The ambitious and innovative programme of exhibitions and displays are designed to transform and enhance the visitors' experience and engagement with the collections. They will be developed as a precursor, and incubator for ideas, leading to the Masterplan. We invite applications for an Exhibitions Project Manager who will be responsible for managing allocated exhibitions and display projects from creative inception through to delivery, across departmental teams and external contributors to an agreed scope and following museum approval stages and reporting procedures. The successful candidate will be assigned to specific projects and will act on initiative and most often independently to identify key issues and drive through activities to a successful and timely conclusion. They will ensure these outputs match the Museum's aspirations and are delivered collaboratively and with rigour, paying close attention to scope, quality, programme and budget. In return, we offer a supportive and inclusive workplace, a generous pension scheme, substantial holiday allowance, and a range of employee benefits, including retail discounts. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Interviews for the role will be held: week commencing 14th September 2026 Please quote reference DA50814 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Exhibition Project Manager Further Particulars Key information Department/location Fitzwilliam Museum Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference DA50814 Category Assistant staff Date published 21 August 2026 Closing date 6 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/finance-analyst-research-and-grants-ew50182": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Finance Analyst - Research and Grants | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Finance Analyst - Research and Grants Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Finance Analyst - Research and Grants The Cambridge Research Office is looking for a number of enthusiastic and motivated individuals to join the Post-Award Team. This is a finance administration role providing support for departments in the management of their research grants. Our team is responsible for providing expert advice and guidance and for financially administering external research funding, on behalf of academics and Departments within the University's Schools. The role provides an excellent opportunity to develop a career in research administration. Your main responsibilities will be providing procedural and financial advice and guidance to academic and departmental staff on a range of financial administration matters. Key tasks include the preparation of final expenditure reports, setting up new awards, preparing invoices and monitoring research grant budgets against expenditure. This is a fast-paced role, requiring the successful candidate to manage a varied workload, balance competing priorities and respond effectively to changing demands. You will demonstrate excellent numeracy, strong organisational skills, a highly collaborative and inquisitive mindset, and a positive, customer-oriented approach. The role holders will be part of a diverse team, working within a busy office environment, so you must be able to prioritise and work to tight deadlines.  Proficiency in using Windows based packages is essential.  Knowledge of Oracle Financials and experience in finance administration would be advantageous. The University is supportive of hybrid working, where some work is undertaken on University premises and some in a remote working environment. The aim of our approach is to enable as many staff as possible to work in a hybrid way if they wish and where their role allows. This role requires onsite attendance at Greenwich House for a minimum of 2 days per week with additional onsite working according to business need. There are several positions available on either a permanent or fixed-term basis (12 months) Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University- 12 months fixed term positions only. Please note that the minimum part-time option for this role is 0.8FTE and applications requesting less than this will not be considered. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please see the Further Particulars document for more details of this vacancy. Your application should clearly set out how you meet the criteria listed in the person specification (the skills and experience required for the role) along with relevant examples. Candidates will be shortlisted based on these criteria. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Applicants who have applied within the last 6 months should not apply during this round. The closing date is Monday 7th September 2026.  Interviews will be held in person in Cambridge around the 18th September 2026. Questions about the application process should be addressed to the Research Office Recruitment team at crorecruitment@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference EW50182 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Cambridge Research Office Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference EW50182 Category Assistant staff Date published 5 August 2026 Closing date 7 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/finance-coordinator-jk50430": {
      "title": "Finance Coordinator",
      "description": "Finance Coordinator | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Finance Coordinator Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Finance Coordinator The Faculty of Law is one of the world's leading institutions for legal research and teaching. We are seeking a proactive and experienced Finance Coordinator to play a key role in supporting the Faculty's financial management and ensuring that financial resources are used effectively to support the Faculty's objectives, academic activities, and strategies. Working closely with a variety of colleagues across the Faculty, you will provide financial advice and management information to support planning and decision-making. You will oversee a wide range of financial activities, including budgeting, forecasting, financial reporting, research grant administration, and compliance with University financial regulations. This is an excellent opportunity for a finance professional who enjoys working collaboratively, analysing complex financial information, and improving processes in a busy, changing, and intellectually stimulating environment. The role offers significant responsibility and variety, with opportunities to contribute to strategic planning, support major academic initiatives, and work with colleagues across the wider University finance community. At present, the University is undergoing an institutional change in its financial processes, practices, and systems. As such, a successful applicant would be expected to play a large role in facilitating the changes, including liaising with central Finance Division colleagues, communicating important information to Faculty staff, and quickly learning new systems. Key responsibilities With the Deputy Faculty Manager (Finance, Research & Facilities Management), produce and analyse management accounts, budgets, forecasts, and financial reports to support effective financial planning and decision-making across the Faculty. Provide financial advice and guidance to a variety of stakeholders within the Faculty, budget holders and colleagues on financial planning, policies and procedures. Monitor income and expenditure, identify financial risks and opportunities, and support the development of financial plans and cost-saving initiatives. With the Research Grants Administrator and relevant academic colleagues, manage and monitor research grant expenditure, providing advice on funding, budgeting and compliance requirements. Ensure Faculty financial procedures comply with University regulations and contribute to the review and improvement of local processes and controls. Maintain the integrity of financial data, undertake reconciliations, investigate discrepancies and support financial reporting requirements. Act as a key liaison with the School of the Humanities & Social Sciences Finance Team, the University's Finance Division and contribute to University-wide finance initiatives and networks. Support and oversee day-to-day finance operations in the Faculty, including purchasing, invoicing, and other financial system processes. Line manage the Faculty's Finance Administrator role, working closely with the position to carry out all functions of the Finance office. About you You will have substantial experience in a finance role, excellent analytical and organisational skills, and the ability to communicate financial information clearly to both financial and non-financial audiences. You will be comfortable working independently, managing competing priorities, and building effective working relationships across a diverse academic community. Experience of financial management within a higher education or similarly complex organisation would be advantageous. The closing date for the role is 23 September 2026. Interviews will take place on 7th October 2026 at the Faculty of Law. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference JK50430 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Faculty of Law Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference JK50430 Category Assistant staff Date published 11 August 2026 Closing date 23 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
