    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/head-radiographer-pp50673": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Head Radiographer | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Head Radiographer Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Head Radiographer Grade 7: £35,608.00 - £46,049.00 per annum An exciting opportunity has arisen for a Head Radiographer to join the Queen's Veterinary School Hospital, Cambridge. With support from the Principal Radiologist, you will provide operational leadership for the Diagnostic Imaging service team within the Queens Veterinary School Hospital (QVSH), an RCVS-accredited teaching and referral hospital providing specialist veterinary care 24 hours a day, 365 days a year. As a key diagnostic service supporting the Hospital's clinical, teaching and research activities, the service delivers advanced imaging for a diverse referral and emergency caseload.  You will also provide advice and support to our primary care practices. Reporting to the Principal Radiologist, the role has operational responsibility for a team of three full-time (including this role) and two part-time Radiographers, working alongside four part-time Radiologists and four Clinical Training Scholars. With support from the Principal Radiologist, the post holder is responsible for the effective delivery, quality and development of the imaging service, ensuring high standards of patient care, radiation safety and operational efficiency. Applicants should not only hold DCR (or equivalent training/experience), but should also have substantial post-graduate experience in radiography at a senior level, including MRI and CT. In addition, applicants should have sound knowledge and understanding of a variety of diagnostic modalities including fluoroscopy, experience of handling small animals, and experience in teaching. The role holder will be required to participate in an out-of-hours rota, to include on-call and weekend working, for which an additional payment is provided. We offer a supportive and engaging environment with generous paid annual leave (41 days including the public holidays). In addition, we are able to provide competitive staff benefits and services, including family-friendly policies, numerous discounts on shopping, health care, financial services, and public transport. We also offer a generous pension scheme, annual CPD allowance and tax-efficient bicycle, car lease and charity-giving schemes. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries please contact Prof. Alice Bird, Associate Hospital Director, by email: arb59@cam.ac.uk Further particulars for the role and information about the Department are available in the Further Particulars document enclosed with this advert. If you are viewing this advert on an external site, please visit the University's job pages for access. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. Please quote reference PP50673 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars - Head Radiographer Key information Department/location Department of Veterinary Medicine Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference PP50673 Category Academic-related Date published 10 August 2026 Closing date 8 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
