      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "HR Manager [Temporary Cover] | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs HR Manager [Temporary Cover] Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs HR Manager [Temporary Cover] The Department of Computer Science and Technology is an academic department that encompasses Computer Science along with many aspects of Technology, Engineering and Mathematics.  With around 340 academic staff, researchers and PhD students, the Department has an international reputation for research excellence and innovation. Our success is built on attracting and supporting talented staff and creating a stimulating environment that promotes a strong sense of community whilst valuing and recognising individual contribution. We are seeking an experienced HR professional to join us as HR Manager on a nine-month fixed-term basis or secondment opportunity, providing cover during the secondment of the current role holder.  The successful candidate will play a key role in supporting the Department through a busy academic year. This is an excellent opportunity for an internal candidate looking to broaden their HR experience and gain exposure to a wide range of people management issues in an active teaching and research department within the School of Technology.  Applications are particularly welcomed from existing University HR professionals looking to further develop their careers. As HR Manager, you will be responsible for providing accurate and timely advice and guidance to staff on HR related matters across the employee lifecycle. In this varied and rewarding role, you will work collaboratively with senior members of the Department to develop, implement and maintain the Department's HR strategy.  You will promote best practice in line with the University's policies and procedures and support areas such as recruitment, probation, staff review and development, capability and sickness absence processes.  Key to your success in this role will be your ability to build and maintain effective working relationships with colleagues at all levels. Previous experience at HR Manager level is not essential, provided candidates can demonstrate the skills and experience required to succeed in the role.  Candidates should, however, have a strong understanding of HR policies, procedures and processes within the University of Cambridge. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. Please quote reference NR50848 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. Please include your CV and a cover letter detailing your suitability for this position. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to: Caroline Stewart,\nDepartmental Secretary at departmental-secretary@cst.cam.ac.uk The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information HR Manager Key information Department/location Department of Computer Science and Technology Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference NR50848 Category Academic-related Date published 27 August 2026 Closing date 16 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
