    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/impact-evaluation-lead-fixed-term-xn50773": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Impact Evaluation Lead (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Impact Evaluation Lead (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Impact Evaluation Lead (Fixed Term) Are you passionate about building evidence that strengthens the role of collections, culture and research to support positive change in society? The University of Cambridge Museums (UCM) is looking for an experienced and collaborative Impact Evaluation Lead to establish a new team working across the University's museums, libraries, archives and Botanic Garden. Together, the University Collections represent the UK's highest concentration of internationally important collections outside London. Through engagement, participation and research, we bring people together to explore the big questions: from the earliest forms of life to the future of our planet. Now we're investing in our ability to understand and evolve the impact of that work. Working across programmes, disciplines and communities, the Impact Evaluation Lead will develop a shared approach to evaluation to better understand the social, cultural and economic impact of participation with collections. You'll manage a specialist team to develop longitudinal approaches to evaluation, build robust datasets and insights, and support colleagues to generate, interpret and act on evidence. About You We're looking for someone with substantial experience of designing and leading evaluation teams working alongside participation and engagement with culture and collections. You'll be confident developing approaches to evaluation that generate meaningful insight over time and across diverse settings. You'll be able to use evidence to shape decision-making, strengthen practice, build capability in others and help embed learning across a complex organisation. You'll bring a strong commitment to socially just and inclusive evaluation practice, with the ability to apply approaches that support participants and communities who are underserved, underrepresented or at risk of marginalisation. If you're excited by the potential of collections, culture and research to create meaningful change, we'd love to hear from you. Benefits of working at Cambridge include: Competitive rates of pay with automatic service-related pay progression and annual cost of living increases Generous annual leave allowance of 41 days paid leave (including bank holidays) Generous maternity, adoption and shared parental leave entitlement and other family friendly schemes (e.g. workplace nurseries and salary exchange schemes for childcare) An auto-enrolment pension scheme, with a generous employer contribution Travel benefits and retail discounts at over 2,000 local and national stores. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please upload your CV and cover letter to the application. Please note that additional uploaded documents will not be considered as part of the recruitment. Informal enquiries about the role should be directed to: David Cahill Roots, Head of UCM Programmes and Collaborations, Email: dc915@cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact Karin Kuchta, HR Coordinator, Email: csihhr@admin.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference XN50773 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information XN50773 - Further Particulars Key information Department/location Cross School Initiative Hub Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference XN50773 Category Academic-related Date published 24 August 2026 Closing date 18 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
