    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/investigator-fixed-term-ah49916": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Investigator (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Investigator (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Investigator (Fixed Term) Two positions are available: one fixed-term post funded for an initial period of 24 months, and one fixed-term maternity cover post for 13.5 months or until the return of the postholder, whichever occurs sooner. We are looking for an experienced Investigator to join the University of Cambridge's Human Resources Division, specialising in complex and sensitive staff investigations.\nThis role plays a key part in ensuring fair, thorough and proportionate investigation processes across a range of staff misconduct and complaint cases. We encourage early applications as they will be reviewed on a rolling basis. The vacancy may close before the advertised deadline if a sufficient number of suitable applications are received. About the role You will lead investigations into a range of staff matters, including complex and sensitive cases such as serious misconduct and complaints, ensuring findings are evidence based and clearly presented. Working closely with HR colleagues and stakeholders, you will provide expert advice, support decision making processes, and contribute to continuous improvement of investigation practices. What you will be doing Managing complex investigations from planning through to final report Interviewing parties, gathering evidence and assessing credibility Producing clear, balanced investigation reports with findings of fact Presenting findings to senior decision makers at hearings Advising stakeholders on investigation processes and risk Delivering training and contributing to improvements in practice We are looking for someone who has Strong experience conducting complex and sensitive investigations Excellent report writing and analytical skills Ability to handle sensitive issues with professionalism and discretion Strong communication and stakeholder management skills Knowledge of UK employment law, investigations and best practice High attention to detail and ability to manage competing priorities Why join us? Alongside working in a collaborative and supportive environment, the University of Cambridge offers a range of excellent benefits, including: Development opportunities such as LinkedIn Learning, job shadowing and career pathways. 41 days annual leave (including bank holidays) and a highly competitive pension scheme. Hybrid working with flexibility in how you arrange your office days. A wide range of discounts at local retailers and thousands of national brands. Health and wellbeing support, including discounted gym access and the Staff Counselling Service. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for flexible working arrangements. For this role, all applications will be managed by Spirehouse Recruitment. To apply, please send your CV to cambridge@spirehouse.co.uk For further information about the role, please contact Abbie Carr (Executive Consultant), abbie@spirehouse.co.uk Closing date: Wednesday 23 September 2026 Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Download further information Investigator - Further Information Document Key information Department/location Human Resources Division Salary £42,254-£56,535 Reference AH49916 Category Academic-related Date published 2 September 2026 Closing date 23 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
