      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Learning Programme Manager (Maternity Cover) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Learning Programme Manager (Maternity Cover) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Learning Programme Manager (Maternity Cover) The Fitzwilliam Museum: Opening up the past to transform our futures. As the principal museum of the University of Cambridge and the largest cultural venue in the region, The Fitzwilliam Museum acts as a crucial bridge between the University, the City and the rest of the world, and has an international reputation for extraordinary research, world class exhibitions, award-winning public programmes and significant collections spanning many cultures and centuries. We invite applications for the role of Learning Programme Manager (Maternity Cover).\nThis role offers an exciting opportunity to develop and deliver the Fitzwilliam's Learning programme, with specific responsibility for the management and development of activity across our schools, young people, and the early years and families programmes. The role oversees the design and practical delivery of exciting, responsive creative learning experiences that will be of interest to a broad spectrum of audiences, including delivery on-gallery, workshops in the studio, self-led trails, family days, resources, creative careers, accredited and non-accredited awards, strategic partnership projects, and training and development for teachers and practitioners, linked to our collections and contributing to our vision and mission. Supported by the Deputy Director, Participation, Learning and Public Programmes, the post holder will work collaboratively with colleagues including the Public Programme Manager and Assistant Research Professor Museum Participation and Practice, to successfully deliver a programme of creative learning for multiple stakeholders. The post directly line manages a team of 7 (3.7FTE), including Learning Associates: Early Years and Families, and Learning Associates: Schools and Teachers, Museum Educators, and programme administrators and assistants, broadening access to the Museum's collection, research and teaching. The post holder is also responsible for leading on the development of new approaches and methodologies to support high-quality, engaging and inclusive creative learning that engages with a diverse range of communities, contributing to ensuring the Museum's collections and the research activities that underpin them become more relevant for a larger and more diverse audience. The role ensures that activity speaks to our four core areas of work within Learning: creating opportunity, identity and society, environment and sustainability, and health and wellbeing, that planned programme outcomes are delivered on time and on budget, that programme impacts are measured and evidenced and that evaluation and consultation feed into continuous improvement to ensure an offer that is high quality and relevant to local need. In practice, the role holder will combine development and direct delivery of programme activity with coordinating, influencing, and inspiring colleagues to contribute to programme delivery to achieve agreed outcomes for audiences. We offer a supportive and inclusive workplace, a generous pension scheme, enhanced family leave, substantial holiday allowance, and a range of employee benefits, including retail discounts. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Temporary cover: This post is fixed-term for 10 months or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Closing date for applications:  6th September 2026 Interviews for the role will be held: 18th September 2026 Please quote reference DA50622 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Learning Programmes Manager (Maternity cover)  Further Particulars Key information Department/location Fitzwilliam Museum Salary £42,254-£56,535 pro rata Reference DA50622 Category Academic-related Date published 5 August 2026 Closing date 6 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/liaison-librarian-cstceb-vi49847": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Liaison Librarian (CST/CEB) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Liaison Librarian (CST/CEB) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Liaison Librarian (CST/CEB) Ever wanted to work in an institution that is home to one of the world's great collections of cultural treasures and research materials? Spanning thousands of years of human thought and discovery, Cambridge University Libraries and Archives house unique treasures and research materials made up of nearly ten million books, maps, manuscripts, photographs and priceless objects.\nThe University of Cambridge Libraries and Archives is a fundamental part of the Cambridge West Innovation District, a dynamic and expanding environment for world-changing research and innovation. At the heart of this vibrant interdisciplinary community is the West Hub, a distinctive space for learning, collaboration, and socialising that reflects a modern University approach to shared resources and integrated library services. The role This is an exciting opportunity for a Liaison Librarian to work with the Cambridge West Team, to support library services across designated departments with responsibilities for teaching, research support and collection development, contributing to the needs of a diverse academic community within an innovative and forward-looking setting. As Liaison Librarian (CST/CEB) you will Deliver library services across the West Cambridge Site. Lead on Academic liaison with the designated Departments. Lead on training sessions in these areas and support colleagues more generally across West Cambridge. Support the West Hub Library Manager to shape library services across Cambridge West based on department's needs. What we are looking for A professional enthusiastic about building and maintaining strong relationships with stakeholders. Experience of developing and delivering training. Enthusiastic about promoting library services through outreach, guidance and personalised support. Proactive and innovative in finding solutions. Flexible to work at and visit multiple buildings. What we offer Flexible working arrangements are available upon discussion. Hybrid working and flexible hours are limited due operational needs. Please do get in contact to discuss if needed. Generous annual leave allowance of 36 days. Exceptional parental leave (including maternity, paternity / co-parent, adoption and shared parental leave). Discounts on major retailers. Professional development opportunities such as apprenticeships and access to a variety of training courses. For further details please refer to the Further Particulars. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. We particularly welcome applications from candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our department. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For informal enquiries please contact Daniele Campello, West Hub Library Manager on dc718@cam.ac.uk Application closing date:  Sunday 6 September 2026. Interview date: Tuesday 22 September 2026 Please quote reference VI49847 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location School of Technology Libraries Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference VI49847 Category Assistant staff Date published 17 August 2026 Closing date 6 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
