    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/liaison-librarian-veterinary-and-pre-clinical-medicine-ve50824": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Liaison Librarian (Veterinary and pre-clinical Medicine) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Liaison Librarian (Veterinary and pre-clinical Medicine) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Liaison Librarian (Veterinary and pre-clinical Medicine) Ever wanted to work in an institution that is home to one of the world's great collections of cultural treasures and research materials? Spanning thousands of years of human thought and discovery, Cambridge University Libraries and Archives house unique treasures and research materials made up of nearly ten million books, maps, manuscripts, photographs and priceless objects. The role We are seeking an experienced, proactive library professional to lead engagement with departments supporting the Pre-clinical Medical and Veterinary Medicine Tripos (MVST). This varied role combines teaching, collection management, and relationship-building to support learning, teaching, and research across the School of Biological Sciences (SBS) As Liaison Librarian (MVST) you will Design and deliver training sessions in partnership with staff and colleagues across SBS and SBS Libraries Teams. Deliver library services across Biological Sciences Libraries. Lead on academic liaison with the designated Departments. Line manage a Senior Library Assistant. Contribute to shared team goals by collaborating effectively and fostering a supportive team culture. What we are looking for Proven ability to develop strong relationships and partnerships with stakeholders. Experience delivering teaching, training, or learning support both online and in-person. Knowledge of academic information resources and databases, with experience in developing user-focused STEM library collections and services. Innovative problem-solver with experience in teamwork and staff supervision. A customer-focused professional with a commitment to excellent service and flexibility to work across multiple sites. What we offer Flexible working arrangements are available upon discussion. Hybrid working and flexible hours are limited due to the operational requirements of the role. If needed, please contact us to discuss. Generous annual leave allowance of 36 days. Exceptional parental leave (including maternity, paternity / co-parent, adoption and shared parental leave). Discounts on major retailers. Professional development opportunities such as apprenticeships and access to a variety of training courses. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. We particularly welcome applications from candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our department. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. For informal enquiries please contact Funmike Ifie, Biological Sciences Librarian.\n Tel: 0776 1044287.    Email: yoi20@cam.ac.uk Application closing date: Monday 7 September 2026. Interview date: Tuesday 29 September 2026 For further details please refer to the Further Particulars. Please quote reference VE50824 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location University Library Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference VE50824 Category Assistant staff Date published 24 August 2026 Closing date 7 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
