    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/llm-and-mcl-admissions-administrator-jk50816": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "LLM and MCL Admissions Administrator | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs LLM and MCL Admissions Administrator Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs LLM and MCL Admissions Administrator The Faculty of Law is seeking to appoint an LLM and MCL Admissions Administrator to join our Professional Services Team. This role provides an exciting opportunity to be part of a supportive Faculty, proactive in providing training and career development opportunities for all staff. The Faculty of Law currently has over 100 University, Faculty and College Teaching Officers. Almost every area of legal interest is represented. Within its professional services team, the Faculty has 25 administrative staff, an IT team of 6. The role holder will provide support to the LLM and MCL Programmes Coordinator for admissions activity within the Faculty in order to provide an efficient admissions experience for prospective students.  The role holder will also provide general administrative support to the LLM and MCL Programmes Coordinator (for those two taught postgraduate programmes). The role holder will provide appropriate support for work undertaken on student information systems i.e. Panel and CamSIS, support circulation of applications to the two degree programmes, support Faculty events held for LLM and MCL students and produce databases and tables of information relating to the programmes. Applicants should have excellent interpersonal and communication skills and a good standard of written and spoken English. The role requires previous administrative experience and excellent IT skills. The role holder must be able to work on their own initiative, in addition to working as part of a team. We offer the flexibility of hybrid working after the probation period and would be willing to discuss this as part of the interview process. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. If you have any questions about this vacancy please contact Suzanne Wade, the LLM and MCL Coordinator at shw27@cam.ac.uk . If you have questions about the application process, please contact the HR office in the Faculty at hr@law.cam.ac.uk The closing date for applications is 27 September 2026. Interviews will be held on 12 October 2026. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference JK50816 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Faculty of Law Salary £27,319-£31,236 Reference JK50816 Category Assistant staff Date published 27 August 2026 Closing date 27 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/marketing-manager-better-futures-ea50737": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Marketing Manager (Better Futures) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Marketing Manager (Better Futures) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Marketing Manager (Better Futures) Are you a strategic marketer who thrives on engaging influential, high-achieving individuals? Do you enjoy crafting tailored, relationship-led marketing approaches rather than mass-market campaigns? The Better Futures Programme, hosted by the University of Cambridge Professional and Continuing Education, is seeking a part-time Marketing Manager to lead the marketing and communications strategy for one of Cambridge's most distinctive leadership programmes. This is a unique opportunity to shape the growth and reputation of a programme that helps accomplished leaders turn a lifetime of achievement into meaningful societal impact. Participants join Better Futures at a significant career and life transition, drawing on the expertise, networks and opportunities of the Cambridge ecosystem to define their next chapter and the difference they want to make in the world. The Role Working closely with the Head of Marketing, you will develop and deliver a marketing and communications strategy that raises awareness and enhances the reputation of the programme. Your focus will be on attracting a diverse pipeline of outstanding applicants, providing the programme with the depth and quality of candidates needed to select an exceptional cohort. Success depends on understanding the motivations of a sophisticated, senior audience and being hands on in delivering targeted, insight-led campaigns that build trust, credibility and engagement. Combining strategic planning with hands-on delivery, you'll lead marketing activity across a variety of channels, while managing specialist suppliers and freelance support. You will play a key role in expanding the programme's profile across the University ecosystem, working collaboratively across Collegiate and departmental networks to influence activity, align priorities, and drive coordinated communications efforts. Ideal Candidate You'll bring: Experience developing and delivering integrated marketing and communications strategies. Experience marketing to senior professional, executive, leadership or high-net-worth audiences where influence, relationships and credibility are critical. Expertise in audience segmentation, customer journeys and targeted communications. Experience managing multi-channel campaigns across digital and traditional channels. Strong stakeholder management skills, with the confidence to engage and influence senior internal and external audiences. Experience planning and delivering high-quality events, networking opportunities or thought leadership activities. An analytical mindset, with experience using data and insight to optimise marketing performance. Benefits 41 days annual leave (pro rata), inclusive of Bank Holidays Defined benefits pension schemes Family-friendly initiatives Career and professional development opportunities Support for health & mental wellbeing Discounts on shopping Rental deposit scheme Public transport season ticket loans Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 2 years in the first instance. This is a part-time role, equivalent to three days per week. We are open to discussion on how these hours are worked, however flexibility is required to attend some occasional evening events. You'll be based at Madingley Hall one day per week and will regularly spend time in central Cambridge supporting programme events and engaging with programme participants. The remainder of your time can be worked remotely. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Further information is available at the link below. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to Alice Bream, Head of Marketing at alice.bream@pace.cam.ac.uk . If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact: HR@pace.cam.ac.uk The closing date for applications is 3 September 2026. Interviews will take place online on 14 September 2026, followed by in-person interviews for shortlisted candidates on 22 September 2026. Please quote reference EA50737 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Marketing Manager Better Futures Key information Department/location University of Cambridge Institute of Professional and Continuing Education Salary £35,608-£46,049 pro rata Reference EA50737 Category Academic-related Date published 13 August 2026 Closing date 3 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/mitigating-circumstances-coordinator-fixed-term-ab50436": {
      "title": "Mitigating Circumstances Coordinator (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Mitigating Circumstances Coordinator (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Mitigating Circumstances Coordinator (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Mitigating Circumstances Coordinator (Fixed Term) Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 31 July 2028 in the first instance. The Team The Exam Operations and Mitigating Circumstances team sit within the Student Administration section of Education Services, supporting the academic purposes of the University.  We provide expert administrative support and advice to the University and Colleges relating to the operational delivery of exams and reasonable adjustments for undergraduate and taught postgraduate courses. We also manage the administration of mitigating circumstances and allowances for undergraduate and taught postgraduate students. About the Role This is a rewarding opportunity to work within an established, supportive team and will be for two years fixed term. The existing Coordinator will be seconded on to an exciting project within the wider exam team. The role is responsible for delivering the administration of examination allowances and adjustments for students by ensuring that applications for examination access arrangements (reasonable adjustments), including adjusted modes of assessment and supporting the examination allowance process for postgraduate students are processed. Given the role requirements, we invite applications from individuals who: have excellent interpersonal and communication skills; have the ability to work collaboratively as well as independently; are positive, approachable and have a diplomatic manner with a wide range of stakeholders; able to foster positive working relationships; are conscientious, will contribute to the continuing success of the team; are motivated and takes initiative; are highly meticulous, accurate and organised; are highly flexible and pro-active in approach; are quick and comfortable to adapt to change; have strong organisational skills and multi-tasking ability. Given the demands of the examination cycle, the role requires a flexible approach to working patterns and the ability to adjust priorities when needed.  Whilst the Exam Team is supportive of hybrid working, there are periods of time where in office working is non-negotiable.  The role holder will be office based during their initial 6-month probation period and for the exam round from April-June.  During this time there will also be some Saturday, evening and Bank Holiday working, for which time off in lieu will be granted. The Exam Team forms part of the Student Administration Service within Education Services and exceptionally, you may be required to work on other tasks within Education Services if there is a change in priorities. Benefits of working at the University of Cambridge include: An opportunity to be part of a large, experienced, supportive and collaborative team; Competitive rates of pay with automatic service-related pay progression and annual cost of living increases; Excellent pension scheme; Generous annual leave allowance Applications are welcome  from both external and internal candidates, including internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. Additional information regarding the role can be found within the Further Particulars. When applying, please upload your CV and cover letter which clearly sets out how you meet the criteria listed in the person specification of the Further Particulars (the knowledge, skills, and experience required for the role) along with relevant examples. Candidates will be shortlisted and invited to interview based upon these criteria. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be initially directed by email to sscjobs@admin.cam.ac.uk The closing date for applications is Wednesday 16 September 2026 The expected, in-person, interviews will be held on Monday 28 or Tuesday 29 September 2026 Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact SSCjobs@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference AB50436 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Student Administration Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference AB50436 Category Academic-related Date published 21 August 2026 Closing date 16 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
