    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/professional-services-support-administrator-fixed-term-internal-applicants-only-ah50914": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Professional Services Support Administrator (Fixed Term) Internal Applicants Only | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Professional Services Support Administrator (Fixed Term) Internal Applicants Only Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Professional Services Support Administrator (Fixed Term) Internal Applicants Only The University of Cambridge is recognised globally as a renowned centre for research, education and scholarship. We employ more than 13,000 staff in a range of academic, research and professional services roles, all of whom play a key role in maintaining and enhancing our world leading reputation. Our people are our greatest asset, and it is critical to our continued success that we create the right conditions for our people to thrive at Cambridge. The Role: The role holder will be deployed as interim cover for absences wherever required across the University.  Assignments will be short (usually three to six months) and may take place across all six Schools and associated central divisions, based on institutional need, the role holder's Department/team will change frequently. What you'll be doing: Managing professional services colleagues Financial and research grant administration Managing the administration of HR related activities Managing the use of office space, overseeing and coordinating maintenance and refurbishments Overseeing health and safety in the office Managing administration projects Representing the administrative office at Senior Management Team meetings as needed We're looking for someone who has: Experience in a senior administrative role Experience of managing staff Advanced knowledge of Higher Education Administration involving a critical understanding of relevant theory and/or principles Excellent organisational skills Ability and confidence to cope with uncertainty and pressured situations Ability to build relationships and establish credibility Further information about the role and its responsibilities is available via the link below. Benefits of working at Cambridge include: Competitive rates of pay with automatic service related pay progression and annual cost of living increases; Generous annual leave allowance of 41 days paid leave (including bank holidays) Flexible and hybrid working opportunities; Generous maternity, adoption and shared parental leave entitlement and other family friendly schemes (e.g. workplace nurseries and salary exchange schemes for childcare); An auto-enrolment pension scheme, with a generous employer contribution; Travel benefits and retail discounts at over 2,000 local and national stores; Schemes to support with relocation / the provision of accommodation The University of Cambridge is committed to supporting our staff to thrive both professionally and personally. We aim to support a good work/life balance, whilst retaining the positive aspects of our unique in-person environment and culture. Elements of this role are suitable for hybrid working, where staff can split their time between in-person collaboration and remote working. The frequency of the remote elements of the role can be discussed with the recruiting manager. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. Applications are welcome from internal candidates who would like to apply for the role on the basis of a secondment from their current role in the University. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. We particularly welcome applications from candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our division. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Closing date for applications: Midnight, Friday 2nd October 2026 Interviews for the role will be held: Friday 16th October 2026 (subject to change) Please quote reference AH50914 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Human Resources Division Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference AH50914 Category Academic-related Date published 1 September 2026 Closing date 2 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/project-coordinator-0-6fte-part-time-fixed-term-jj50860": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator 0.6FTE (Part Time, Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Project Coordinator 0.6FTE (Part Time, Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Project Coordinator 0.6FTE (Part Time, Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Project Coordinator 0.6FTE (Part Time, Fixed Term) The Faculty of History wishes to recruit a part time Project Coordinator.  This role will be a fixed term, 0.6 FTE position for 50 months until 30 November 2030 and will support the day-to-day organization of Professor Regina Grafe's ERC AdvGrant project 'COFILA, Colonial credit and financial diversity in the Global South: Spanish America 1600-1820s'. The Project Coordinator will co-ordinate the efficient running of the research project, create and maintain documents and the project website in the two project languages (English and Spanish),  assist Professor Grafe's supervision of academic staff and their research work, and the project's budget and logistics in order to ensure the smooth running and that the project successfully meets ERC standards of academic excellence. This is a varied and challenging role and  we are looking for someone with administrative experience,  who is fluent in Spanish oral and written language skills demonstrated by a Spanish language qualification or relevant practical experience. You will be educated to degree level/Level 6 or with an equivalent level of practical experience. You will have an advanced knowledge of project coordination theories  and be experienced in using Microsoft 365. You will also have  excellent planning, organisational, interpersonal and communication skills.  Alongside strong research, analysis and reporting skills and some experience working in the humanities; you will have an ability to keep, monitor and update data, create and maintain websites, and assist with the editing and publication of research as required. In addition you will have the capacity for independent working and problem solving, as well as co-operative team-building skills. You will have a proactive and flexible approach and experience in an administrative/project role. Experience of working in a Higher Education environment is desirable. More information about the Faculty can be found here: https://www.hist.cam.ac.uk/ Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 30 November 2030 in the first instance. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to: Professor Regina Grafe - rg752@cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact - hr@hist.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference JJ50860 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Faculty of History Salary £33,951-£39,906 pro rata Reference JJ50860 Category Assistant staff Date published 25 August 2026 Closing date 13 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/project-grant-manager-fixed-term-ps50871": {
      "title": "Your cookie choices",
      "description": "Project Grant Manager (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Project Grant Manager (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Project Grant Manager (Fixed Term) The UK Hub for Predictive and AI-Enabled Human Disease Models is a UK national research initiative funded by MRC, which will translate academic New Approach Methodologies (NAMs) into validated, industry-ready systems. The Hub brings together leading scientists, clinicians and commercial organisations to drive advances for national benefit. The Hub is based in the Cambridge Stem Cell Institute (CSCI).\nThe Project Grant Manager will provide comprehensive operational & financial management for the UKRI National Hub (£25M). They will ensure effective delivery of a complex, multi-partner research and innovation programme and will be responsible for coordinating grant administration, financial monitoring, reporting, governance, and compliance across the Hub. We are seeking a proactive and highly organised Project Grant Manager to play a central role in the delivery and development of this ambitious programme. This is a dynamic and visible position at the heart of a high-impact research environment. The post holder will work closely with the Hub Senior Programme Manager, Directors, collaborators and partner organisations. They will support the coordination of scientific, operational, financial and strategic activities. Key Responsibilities Coordinate the operational delivery of the UK Hub Coordinate the Hub's portfolio of translational research activities Provide high-level project management support to the Hub leadership team Manage the Hub's financial resources Develop & maintain effective relationships with stakeholders Lead governance & reporting activities Support development & implementation of processes to enhance Hub effectiveness Ensure compliance with University policies, UKRI requirements, & relevant legislative & regulatory frameworks. The successful candidate will hold a first degree in in a relevant discipline, or equivalent professional experience and have experience of managing complex projects or programmes, including planning, delivery, monitoring progress, & achieving objectives within agreed timescales & budgets. A recognised project management qualification (e.g. PRINCE2 Practitioner, APM Project Management Qualification, or equivalent) or a willingness to work towards one is desirable. They will be comfortable operating in a fast-paced academic environment and able to engage effectively with a wide range of stakeholders, including researchers, clinicians, funders, and external partners. This is an opportunity to contribute directly to this new national Hub and the role offers significant scope to shape how the Hub will operate, connect, and grow, both within Cambridge and across the UK. Full-time (1.0 FTE; change to part time and flexible working arrangements available); Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 31 March 2030 in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and a CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. The closing date for applications is: 24th September 2026 The interview date for the role is: To be confirmed Please quote reference PS50871 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars - PS50871 (final) Key information Department/location Cambridge Stem Cell Institute (SBS) Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference PS50871 Category Academic-related Date published 26 August 2026 Closing date 24 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/purchasing-assistant-ka49172": {
      "title": "Purchasing Assistant",
      "description": "Purchasing Assistant | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Purchasing Assistant Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Purchasing Assistant The Department of Physics has recently re-located to our new research facility, the Ray\nDolby Centre. Designed to match the most exacting standards of current research,\nserving the educational needs of future generations of undergraduate and graduate\nstudents. To support the Department's operational and research requirements, the dedicated\nPurchasing team now uses Jira, an advanced request management system. The\nforthcoming implementation of Oracle Fusion as the University's new Finance system is\nexpected to further enhance the Department's purchasing and procurement capabilities. We are seeking a motivated and enthusiastic individual to join our Finance team\n(Purchasing Function). Whether you already have experience or are looking to begin a\nlong term career in procurement, this is an excellent opportunity to develop your skills\nin a supportive, modern working environment that supports employee wellbeing and offers a friendly, team orientated culture. Reporting to a Purchasing Administrator in the team, you will undertake a range of\npurchasing and procurement duties within the Department's Finance office following\nUniversity policy and procedures and best practice. The role-holder will ensure that all\npurchasing adheres to best practice and guidelines issued by the University Procurement Service. The successful candidate will be able to work effectively with multiple stakeholder\ngroups, including academic, technical and administrative staff and students, to deliver\nefficient ways to source goods and services for the wide range of activities undertaken\nby the Department. They will be educated to at least 'A' level standard or with\nequivalent level of practical experience and be confident in providing accurate and\ntimely response to customer requests, with excellent communication and organisational skills. The Role You will provide direct purchasing support to the Department, including: Work as part of a team of buyers to process purchasing transactions on CUFS, the\nUniversity's finance system Handle incoming queries on purchasing and related matters Preparing activity and spend reports using tools including CUFS and COGNOS, and identify opportunities to improve workflow Provide guidance and assistance to stakeholders sourcing goods and services in line with best practice and University regulations, maintain documentation covering local procedures Your Skills Have experience of working in a busy purchasing or finance function within a large organisation. Confident and experienced in working on projects with multiple stakeholder groups. Highly numerate and have good oral and written communication skills. Skilled in dealing with financial or procurement controls and able to prioritise your own workload. The Cavendish is supportive of Hybrid working and following completion of a\nprobationary period, operates an 'in more than out' policy. All Hybrid working is subject to operational requirements. We encourage early applications as they will be reviewed on a rolling basis. The vacancy may close before the advertised deadline if a sufficient number of suitable applications are received. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to: Dmitrii Buravlev at db996@cam.ac.uk .  If you have any questions about the application process, please contact hr@phy.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference KA49172 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Physics Salary £27,319-£31,236 Reference KA49172 Category Assistant staff Date published 10 August 2026 Closing date 7 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
