      "description": "Research Assistant (Internal Only) (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant (Internal Only) (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant (Internal Only) (Fixed Term) Applications are invited for a full-time Research Assistant to support ongoing research projects investigating the biological and psychological causes and mechanisms of psychosis. The successful candidate will join Professor Murray's group (CPPDS https://www.cppds.org.uk/ ) within the department of Psychiatry. The successful candidate will support the following studies: -VOLABIOS: EU-funded VOLABIOS project aims to enhance schizophrenia management via the detection of volatile organic compounds (VOCs) in breath, urine, blood and skin as non-invasive biomarkers for early diagnosis. The project will conduct clinical studies involving subjects across six centres and a blind validation study with at-risk individuals. https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/101156162 -The Mental Health Mission for Psychosis: a multi-disciplinary, multi-centre, UK wide collaboration involving Universities, NHS Trust and healthcare companies. The focus is to understand more about patients with early psychosis to help enable better prevention and treatment. The project is funded by the Office of Life Science and National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR). https://eim.digitrial.com/ The proportion of time spent on each programme will be discussed with the successful applicants. Applicants should have a degree in psychology, neuroscience, linguistics or a related discipline. Experience of participant recruitment is essential. Experience of working with people with psychosis is desirable. Excellent organisational and communication skills are required. The successful candidate must have prior experience in participant recruitment and data collection. For further details, please read the further particulars, please provide at least 3 references, a CV and covering letter indicating how you meet the criteria for this post. Informal enquiries are encouraged and may be directed to Professor Graham Murray, gm285@cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact Simon Gurry, HR Coordinator ( hradminpsychiatry@medschl.cam.ac.uk ) . Deadline for applications is  6th September, with interviews in person on the 16th September. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application.\nPlease include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference RN50839 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particular Key information Department/location Department of Psychiatry Salary £33,002-£35,608 Reference RN50839 Category Research Date published 24 August 2026 Closing date 6 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
