    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-assistant-in-advanced-manufacturing-and-materials-grade-nm50665": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in Advanced Manufacturing and Materials Grade",
      "description": "Research Assistant in Advanced Manufacturing and Materials Grade | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant in Advanced Manufacturing and Materials Grade Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant in Advanced Manufacturing and Materials Grade A position exists, for a Research Assistant in the Department of Engineering, to work on Advanced Manufacturing and Materials. The post holder will be located in Central Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, UK. The key responsibilities and duties are: Undertake basic research; for example, by preparing, setting up, conducting and recording the outcome of laser powder bed fusion, mechanical testing, and/or microstructure analysis of metal samples. Custodianship of specific instrumentation, including upgrades, calibration, maintenance and performance checks. Continue to update knowledge, develop skills, and adapt to new research directions and equipment set up in the research group. Analyse and interpret the results of own research and generate original ideas based on outcomes; and contribute to the production of research reports and publications. Develop laboratory protocols of best practice and contribute to a safe and organised research environment, including organising and stocking of consumables. Assist in the supervision of student projects. Make internal and external contacts to develop knowledge and understanding and form relationships for future collaboration, co-ordinate own work with that of others to avoid conflict, and contribute to the planning of research projects. The skills, qualifications and experience required to perform the role are: A Bachelor Degree in Mechatronics/Mechanical Engineering/Materials Science or equivalent Working knowledge of Matlab/Python or equivalent. Experience with programming microcontrollers and with machine learning/AI is a plus. Being familiar with laser powder bed fusion processes. A proven ability to communicate with academic and industrial partners both in speaking and in writing. Ability to manage own workload and to work on multiple tasks in parallel. Salary Range: \nResearch Assistant: £33,002 - £35,608 Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 12 months in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you submit your Curriculum Vitae (CV), a 1-page covering letter to describe how your profile matches the job requirements, and names and contact details of at least 2 referees who could provide a recommendation letter on your behalf. Documents should be uploaded in the Upload section of the online application. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please submit your application by midnight on the closing date. If you have any questions about this vacancy or the application process, please contact: Elizabeth Howard, Divisional Coordinator, eh301@cam.ac.uk Please quote reference NM50665 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Department of Engineering Salary £33,002-£35,608 Reference NM50665 Category Research Date published 6 August 2026 Closing date 3 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-assistantpostdoctoral-research-associate-fixed-term-su50576": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/*Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Assistant/*Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Assistant/*Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Assistant/*Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fixed Term) We are looking for a post-doctoral research associate with an interest in understanding and improving perception of speech by people who hear using a Cochlear Implant. This is a fixed-term post with funds available for 2 years, funded by the Evelyn Trust. Many users of Cochlear Implants understand speech in quiet conditions, but struggle in noisy situations. This is partly because Cochlear Implants can stimulate too many neurons at once, making it difficult to perceive the fine details in everyone's voices. The successful candidate will work on a research project evaluating current-focusing methods to reduce channel interactions and improve speech perception with Cochlear Implants. Questions to be addressed are: (i) What is the optimal neural excitation pattern for each electrode of a Cochlear Implant so as to minimise channel interactions and improve speech perception? (ii) What is the best way to achieve that pattern? (iii) How much does this vary across Cochlear-Implant users? These questions will be addressed with a series of behavioural and electro-physiological experiments with Cochlear Implant users, as well as comparing the outcomes with predictions from existing computational models of the auditory nerve. The successful candidate will be working with Dr François Guérit, as well as collaborating with leading scientists at the MRC Cognition and Brain Sciences Unit (Dr Robert P. Carlyon, Dr Charlotte Garcia) and the Department of Clinical Neurosciences (Pr Manohar Bance and Pr Deborah Vickers). The successful candidate will be based at the MRC Cognition and Brain Sciences Unit (MRC CBU). The successful candidate will have or be about to receive a PhD in a relevant subject area such as, but not limited to psychology, cognitive neuroscience, engineering, physiology, or audiology. Experience in performing behavioural or EEG experiments with Cochlear Implant users, experience in a high-level programming language, and proven willingness and ability to learn new technical skills are highly desirable for this post. See the Further Particulars document for more details. Questions about this role can be addressed to Dr François Guérit, francois.guerit@mrc-cbu.cam.ac.uk . This appointment requires a Research Passport application. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Applicants must have (or be close to obtaining) a PhD. Appointment at *Research Associate level is dependent on having a PhD. Those who have submitted but not yet received their PhD will initially be appointed as a Research Assistant (Grade 5, Point 38 £34,610) moving to Research Associate (Grade 7) upon confirmation of your PhD award. Please ensure that you upload a covering letter and CV in the Upload section of the online application. The covering letter should outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role. If you upload any additional documents which have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Closing Date: 14th September 2026 Interview Date: to be confirmed Please quote reference SU50576 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location MRC Cognition and Brain Sciences Unit Salary £34,610 - £35,608 £37,694 - £46,049 Reference SU50576 Category Research Date published 14 August 2026 Closing date 14 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
