      "title": "Research Associate (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Associate (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Associate (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Associate (Fixed Term) Applications are invited for a highly motivated post-doctoral research associate to join Prof Uta Paszkowski's group at the Crop Science Centre, starting on 1st October 2026. The successful candidate will be joining a vibrant and friendly group of researchers in the Crop Science Centre at the University of Cambridge. The Crop Science Centre which opened in October 2020 benefits from the diverse skills and expertise of the University of Cambridge and NIAB, providing an environment for research excellence in crops, with the drive and expertise for scientific translation to address real-world problems. CRISPR/Cas gene editing is a pioneering technology for precision crop improvement. However, its application in many crops remains constrained by the reliance on genetic transformation, a labour-intensive and technically challenging process. Virus-induced gene editing (VIGE), in which components of the gene-editing machinery are delivered via viral vectors, offers a promising alternative that could significantly broaden the applicability of gene editing in crops. This project aims to establish VIGE in the underutilised African legume Bambara groundnut, with the overarching goal of accelerating genetic improvement of this crop for use in Sub-Saharan Africa. Applicants should possess a strong background in plant virology, plant genetics, and molecular biology. Prior experience with virus-induced gene editing is essential. Experience in basic bioinformatics would be advantageous. Appointment at Research Associate level is dependent on having a PhD. Those who have submitted but not yet received their PhD will be appointed at Research Assistant level, which will be amended to Research Associate once the PhD has been awarded. We welcome a diversity of applicants with a good track record in research and/or impact, who are excited to join a dynamic team of scientists Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 18 months. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have not received any response 1 month after the closing date you should consider your application to be unsuccessful. Please quote reference PD50850 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Plant Sciences Salary £34,610  £35,608 £37,694  £46,049 Reference PD50850 Category Research Date published 25 August 2026 Closing date 8 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
