    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-associate-fixed-term-ge50790": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Associate (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Associate (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Associate (Fixed Term) Applications are sought for three Research Associates to join the Cambridge Lab for Ancient World Studies (CLAWS), directed by Professor Josephine Quinn. Starting no later than 1 October 2027, you will anchor a new phase of activities for the Lab focusing on ancient entanglements in the broadest senses. As well as supporting CLAWS events and administration, you will conduct your own research project(s) within the broad themes of the Centre, addressing at least two different regions and/or periods and/or languages. One project will relate to semitic languages and cultures, broadly construed. A second will relate to archaeology, broadly construed, and cognate subjects. A third is open-field with respect to Ancient World Studies. Candidates may be considered for one, two, or all three positions. The appointments have been made possible with the support of the Faculties of Classics, Asian & Middle Eastern Studies, and History, as well as the McDonald Institute for Archaeological Research, and further details about the major co-funders may be found in the further particular document. Candidates will need to show evidence of the following qualifications, skills and experience: Doctorate in a relevant discipline (or clear evidence that the award of such a doctorate is imminent) Expertise in one or more areas of ancient world studies, including but not limited to semitic languages and cultures and/or archaeology and cognate subjects Relevant expertise and training to successfully carry out the proposed research project Willingness and ability to develop academic interests in new topics, regions, periods, and/or languages Record of relevant research publications (or evidence that such publications are in progress) commensurate with stage of career Ability to work as part of a team. In order for your application to be considered, please ensure you upload the following: Cover letter CV, including a list of publications Statement of max. 500 words in total summarizing (a) the significance of your current and existing research in relation to the aims and activities of CLAWS and (b) the research project you propose to undertake at Cambridge Full description of proposed research project (up to 1000 words, including bibliography) Sample(s) of academic work (up to 10,000 words with a preference for published work) Names and contact details of two academic referees who have agreed to provide references. These will be requested later in the process If you have any queries regarding the application process please contact the School HR Team on sahhr@admin.cam.ac.uk . The closing date for applications is midnight (BST) on Thursday 8 October 2026. Interviews are planned for Thursday 26 November 2026, subject to confirmation. The funds for this post are available for 2 years in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference GE50790 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Faculty of Classics Salary £37,694-£46,049 Reference GE50790 Category Research Date published 27 August 2026 Closing date 8 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
