    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/research-associate-fixed-term-pk50877": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Research Associate (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Associate (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Associate (Fixed Term) We wish to recruit a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Scientist to join the laboratory of Prof Adrian Liston and Prof James Dooley within the Department of Pathology, University of Cambridge ( https://www.listonlab.uk/ ). Employment will be at the G7 Research Associate level at the University of Cambridge. The project is based on understanding gut-resident regulatory T cells. The project will include in vivo CrispR screening and retrogenic TCR analysis of regulatory T cells in the mouse gut. The work aims to understand the basic biology of regulatory T cell tissue homing and residency in the gut, during health and disease. The experiments will take one year. The ideal candidate would have knowledge of regulatory T cell biology and experience in managing ambitious projects. Candidates must have a PhD in immunology or the related biological sciences, and a track record of research achievements. Knowledge of in vivo mouse immunology, including procedures and high dimensional flow cytometry is essential. We seek collegiate applicants who enjoy being part of a team and are committed to maintaining the positive and inclusive research culture that exists in our laboratory. Fixed-term: The post is available as a 1-year fixed term position in the first instance with a negotiable starting date and subject to a 6-month probationary period. Opportunities will be available for motivated candidates to apply for fellowships or contribute to grant applications for extended stays. Historically, of the ~30 post-doctoral researchers who have joined the laboratory, when they have left our lab 27% have gone on to tenure-track academic positions, 27% have gone on to another post-doc position, and 42% have gone on to positions in biotech or pharma. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment. Please ensure that you upload your Curriculum Vitae (CV) and a motivation letter including career development plans in the upload section of the online application. Please provide contact details, including an email address for two referees. At least one of your referees should be someone who is familiar with your work in your primary research field. If you upload any additional documents that have not been requested, we will not be able to consider these as part of your application. The position is based within the Division of Immunology in the Department of Pathology. The Division offers a highly collaborative and collegiate environment, with advanced scientific facilities in the centre of Cambridge. We host an external seminar series as well as internal talks, journal clubs. There are approximately 40 research groups spanning a wide array of disciplines, including infectious and genetic diseases, immunology and cancer biology. Additional information can be found at https://www.path.cam.ac.uk/research/immunology-division Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries and requests for further information are very welcome and should be addressed to Prof Liston al989@cam.ac.uk If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact: hr@path.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference PK50877 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Department of Pathology Salary £37,694-£46,049 Reference PK50877 Category Research Date published 27 August 2026 Closing date 10 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
