      "description": "Teaching Associate in Computational Linguistics (Temporary Cover) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Teaching Associate in Computational Linguistics (Temporary Cover) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Teaching Associate in Computational Linguistics (Temporary Cover) The Department of Theoretical and Applied Linguistics is seeking to appoint a part-time Teaching Associate (0.5FTE) in Computational Linguistics. This role is to provide temporary cover until 30 September 2027. Educated to a PhD level, the role holder will have core technical expertise in Computational Linguistics and Natural Language Processing. Successful candidates will have prior experience of teaching delivery in this area and excellent presentation and communication skills. The role holder will be expected to contribute to the teaching, research supervision and examining for the MPhil in Linguistics and Language Sciences. They will also contribute to some teaching, supervision and examining for the Department's undergraduate course in Linguistics. They will work with the Postgraduate Administrator to monitor student attainment, wellbeing and feedback, and undertake administrative duties commensurate with the grade of the role. The successful candidate will be based at the Department of Theoretical and Applied Linguistics which is part of the Faculty of Modern and Medieval Languages and Linguistics. The department offers excellent theoretical and empirical research in a broad spread of fields form historical linguistics and comparative syntax to language processing and computational linguistics. It also houses the Language Technology Laboratory which conducts research in the areas of Computational Linguistics and Natural Language Processing. More information about the Department can be found at: https://www.mmll.cam.ac.uk/subjects/theoretical-and-applied-linguistics In order for your application to be considered, please upload the following documents: Covering letter Curriculum vitae, including a list of publications One article or chapter-length writing sample (max 10,000 words) Names and contact details of two referees who are familiar with your work in the relevant field. Temporary cover: This post is fixed-term until 30 September 2027 or the return of the post holder, whichever is the earlier. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any questions about this vacancy, you can contact Professor Anna Korhonen alk23@cam.ac.uk . If you have questions about the application process, please contact the School HR Team on MMLLPersonnel@admin.cam.ac.uk The closing date for applications is midnight (BST) on Tuesday 15 September 2026. Interviews will be held in the week commencing 28 September 2026, subject to change. Please quote reference GN50797 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Department of Theoretical and Applied Linguistics Salary £35,608-£46,049 pro rata Reference GN50797 Category Academic Date published 1 September 2026 Closing date 15 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
